{"page":24,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.19833,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"10 Chapter 1: Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09309,"w":0.59305,"h":0.07503,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"Algebraic Functions Any function constructed from polynomials using algebraic oper- ations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, and taking roots) lies within the class of algebraic functions. All rational functions are algebraic, but also included are more complicated functions (such as those satisfying an equation like y3 - 9xy + x3 = 0, studied in Section 3.7). Figure 1.20 displays the graphs of three algebraic functions."},{"x":0.41482,"y":0.1944,"w":0.11964,"h":0.01257,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"y y = x1\u00073(x − 4)"},{"x":0.8015,"y":0.20207,"w":0.07477,"h":0.01257,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y = x(1 − x)2\u00075"},{"x":0.58642,"y":0.2142,"w":0.08442,"h":0.02152,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"y = (x2 − 1)2\u00073 3 4"},{"x":0.40833,"y":0.22209,"w":0.00654,"h":0.05379,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"1 2 3 4"},{"x":0.39257,"y":0.28542,"w":0.08004,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"4 −1"},{"x":0.57917,"y":0.28542,"w":0.22059,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"1 1 −1 0"},{"x":0.78381,"y":0.2865,"w":0.00491,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.00767,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"5 7"},{"x":0.40095,"y":0.29467,"w":0.01392,"h":0.03926,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"−3 −2 −1"},{"x":0.74609,"y":0.31281,"w":0.01392,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−1"},{"x":0.61785,"y":0.35818,"w":0.01591,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(b)"},{"x":0.77546,"y":0.35818,"w":0.01453,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(c)"},{"x":0.43697,"y":0.35842,"w":0.01453,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(a)"},{"x":0.35464,"y":0.38255,"w":0.31443,"h":0.01228,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 1.20 Graphs of three algebraic functions."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.41996,"w":0.593,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Trigonometric Functions The six basic trigonometric functi